          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Optimum Nutrition Gold Standard 100% Whey is the better whey of the two: leaner at about 77% protein by weight, isolate-led, banned-substance tested with an NSF Certified for Sport listing, and cheaper per 25 g of protein on Amazon at the prices we saw. Body Fortress Super Advanced Whey answers back with a bigger 30 g scoop and, off a Walmart shelf, a price near $1 per 25 g that Gold Standard cannot match.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            So shop by where you buy. Online, pick Gold Standard in the 5 lb or 10 lb tub. In a big-box store, Body Fortress is a sound budget whey if you are fine with concentrate, maltodextrin and two artificial sweeteners. If you are a tested athlete, or concentrate upsets your stomach, Gold Standard or its isolate is the safer choice either way.
          </p>
